 "lines": {
  "hook": "What happens if you drink too much water?",
  "b1": "Your kidneys can only clear about a liter of water an hour.",
  "b2": "Drink faster than that, and the sodium in your blood gets diluted.",
  "b3": "Water then moves into your cells, and they start to swell.",
  "b4": "In the brain, that swelling can cause headaches and confusion.",
  "b5": "Long-distance runners who drink too much are especially at risk.",
  "end": "How much water do you drink a day?"
 },
